{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310575,"nonce":"YXc0UuBd2TOaWeSKy289u3N1Ym4=","title":"FIXED ca707495 (542-\u003e547): (1) a method overridden in ANOTHER module was called directly on the base (Output.writeByte); (2) `n \u0026 0x8000 != ...","message":"**ONE CHAIN, 2026-09-19, found by following `BytesOutput.writeInt32`:**\n\n1. **Cross-module virtual dispatch never existed.** `build_class_vtables`\n   made a method virtual only when an `override` was visible in the module\n   being lowered; a base compiled as a dependency (Output.hx) called its\n   own body (`throw NotImplemented`). And in the SUBCLASS's module the\n   imported parent had no `class_method_by_name` entries → no vtable at\n   all (`PosException.toString`, `EnumValueMap.copy` — all silently direct).\n   Fix: `StaticSigIndex` (fed by EVERY parse, incl. the import loader's\n   discovery parse — added `index_file` there) records `override`s;\n   `is_overridden_below(class, m)` seeds the base's slot; a subclass whose\n   parent isn't lowered here (`class_parent_map` empty = Placeholder\n   parent) lays its table out from `index_slot_layout` (ancestors root\n   first, NAME order); vtables are `Vec\u003cOption\u003cSymbolId\u003e\u003e` and the RUNTIME\n   inherits unset slots via RTTI `super_type_id` (`inherit_vtable_slots`).\n   GENERIC classes are EXEMPT from seeding: the vtable would hold the\n   erased body (BalancedTree\u003cString,Int\u003e.compare broke, suite caught it).\n2. **Precedence:** RD table and legacy chain both had C's ladder. Haxe:\n   `%` \u003e `* /` \u003e `+ -` \u003e shifts \u003e `\u0026 | ^` (ONE level) \u003e comparisons \u003e `...`\n   \u003e `\u0026\u0026` \u003e `||` \u003e `??`. Legacy chain now: equality → relational →\n   `bitwise_expr` → shift; `|`/`\u0026` must refuse the first char of `||`/`\u0026\u0026`.\n3. **If-join skipped parameters**: `var_initial_values` came from\n   `func.locals`; a parameter has none (loops already had the fallback to\n   `get_register_type`). Every `if (x == null) x = default` was broken.\n4. **Placeholder parent = no reserved slots**: `collect_inherited_fields`\n   now takes `instance_field_count(parent)` from the index. Same family:\n   a SETTER on a placeholder parent links by `Declaring.set_x` forward ref\n   (walk `parent_of` until `declares_instance_method`).\n5. **Int64**: mapping comment said the two-word stdlib impl \"is never\n   compiled\" — it was, for every unmapped method. `___Int64`/`__Int64`/\n   `Int64` (they share a root symbol) convert to I64; `.high/.low` on any\n   Int64-typed receiver OR a field owned by `haxe.___Int64` (inlined\n   getter) → `Int64_getHigh/Low`; `new ___Int64` → `Int64_make`; `this` of\n   an Int64 method is the i64 (signatures.rs forced `*void`).\n   Also: `@:op` now checked against operand types (`Int32 + String` took\n   `add(Int32,Int32)`); qualified path `haxe.Int64.make` accepted only\n   Class|Enum symbols.\n6. Inline `#elseif` chains in the preprocessor (`#else` is a PREFIX of\n   `#elseif`); `rayzor.Bytes` gained `new(len, Array\u003cInt\u003e)` + `getData()`.\n\n**TRAPS:** `haxe_reflect_compare_typed` must be declared `-\u003e i64` at every\nsite (two signatures under one JIT name = \"can't resolve symbol\nX__extern_N\" on ~270 rows). A probe reading 3 bytes then `readInt32` throws\nEof — that was MY probe, not the compiler.\n\nSTILL OPEN in the family: `import haxe.Int64.*` wildcard statics\n(TestInt64), `pkg.Module.SubType.field` paths (TestBasetypes), `Rest.of`\narray access (Issue10909), `Null\u003cT\u003e` with T=Int64 (Issue4842), default\narg values (TestDefaultArgs), `Std.string(map)`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_cross_module_vtable_and_haxe_precedence` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}